  (text "I/O on J1 (Harness sheet): AIN1 = J1 pin 9 (sensor return: J1 pin 2), DOUT1 = J1 pin 10; sensor 5 V from J1 pin 11 (200 mA via F801). NOT isolated: GND is the supply ground (vehicle battery negative).\nAIN1: 0-30 V measured (abs. max +/-60 V continuous), input resistance 110 kOhm. 2 x 49.9k 0.1 % 1206 in series (shares a 600 V pulse) / 10k 0.1 %: ratio 0.0911, 30 V -> 2.73 V.\n  ADS1115 (I2C 0x48, AIN0) PGA ranges: +/-4.096 V -> 0-36 V (VDD-limited), +/-1.024 V -> 0-11.2 V, +/-0.512 V -> 0-5.6 V. 100nF + 9.1 kOhm = 0.9 ms filter.\n  C901 is rated 1 kV: it sits on the pin, where ISO 7637 pulse 1 (-600 V) lands. BAV99 (nA leakage; a Schottky's would offset small readings when hot) shares the clamp current with the ADS1115 input diodes.\n  R904 (not fitted): fit 120R 0.1 % 1206 for a 4-20 mA sensor (0.48-2.4 V). Leave it empty for voltage sensors: with it fitted, 24 V on AIN1 burns 4.8 W.\nDOUT1: open-drain low-side switch, BSP75N self-protected MOSFET: 0.5 A continuous for 12/24 V loads (relay coil, buzzer, lamp) wired from +V to DOUT1.\n  60-75 V active clamp (inductive kick without flyback diode, 24 V load dump), current limit 0.7-1.5 A, thermal shutdown with auto restart, off-state leakage 15 uA max at 32 V.\n  GPIO23 -> 74AHCT1G125 on +5V (BSP75N protection needs VIN >= 4.5 V). R905 100k keeps DOUT1 off during reset and boot. Active high: GPIO23 = 1 -> DOUT1 on (sinks to GND)."
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "c254fa94-61a2-41f5-a6cc-97a5060ea7db")
  )
